<title>UK: Abbey to make firm bid for ScotAm Friday.</title>
<headline>Abbey to make firm bid for ScotAm Friday.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank Abbey National said on Thursday it would make a firm offer for mutually-owned life assurer Scottish Amicable on Friday according to the timetable set out by ScotAm.  </p>
<p>Abbey chairman Lord Tugendhat said the firm bid would follow the bank's study of financial data provided by ScotAm.</p>
<p>The Abbey's preliminary offer for ScotAm at the end of January put the price of the life assurer at up to 1.4 billion stg but that bid was trumped by Prudential corp which came in at around 1.9 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
